{
  "_comment": [
    "Running-example context for the Signaling Apple code check.",
    "The docs' per-step fragments assume the surrounding sample from the same page:",
    "properties on the view model / view controller, and helper methods such as",
    "addToMessageList. Declaring them here lets a fragment compile on its own.",
    "",
    "A stub is emitted ONLY when the block does not declare the same symbol itself,",
    "so a block that defines `var rtmKit` is never flagged for redeclaration.",
    "",
    "Keep this list minimal. Every stub is a compile error the harness chooses not",
    "to see, so anything added here should be a symbol the page genuinely defines",
    "elsewhere, not a way to paper over a missing declaration in the docs."
  ],

  "swift": {
    "imports": ["Foundation", "Combine", "SwiftUI", "UIKit", "AgoraRtmKit"],
    "macosImports": [
      "Foundation",
      "Combine",
      "SwiftUI",
      "AppKit",
      "AgoraRtmKit"
    ],
    "fileLevel": [
      "struct Message: Identifiable, Equatable { let id = UUID(); var content: String = \"\" }"
    ],
    "members": [
      { "name": "appid", "code": "var appid: String = \"\"" },
      { "name": "token", "code": "var token: String = \"\"" },
      { "name": "rtmKit", "code": "var rtmKit: AgoraRtmClientKit? = nil" },
      {
        "name": "rtm",
        "code": "var rtm: AgoraRtmClientKit! = nil"
      },
      {
        "name": "rtmClient",
        "code": "var rtmClient: AgoraRtmClientKit! = nil"
      },
      { "name": "username", "code": "@Published var username: String = \"\"" },
      { "name": "message", "code": "@Published var message: String = \"\"" },
      { "name": "channel", "code": "@Published var channel: String = \"\"" },
      { "name": "messages", "code": "@Published var messages: [Message] = []" },
      {
        "name": "addToMessageList",
        "code": "func addToMessageList(str: String) {}"
      },
      { "name": "initializeEngine", "code": "func initializeEngine() {}" },
      { "name": "login", "code": "func login() {}" },
      { "name": "logout", "code": "func logout() {}" },
      { "name": "subscribe", "code": "func subscribe() {}" },
      { "name": "unsubscribe", "code": "func unsubscribe() {}" },
      { "name": "sendMessage", "code": "func sendMessage() {}" }
    ]
  },

  "objc": {
    "imports": [
      "<Foundation/Foundation.h>",
      "<UIKit/UIKit.h>",
      "<AgoraRtmKit/AgoraRtmKit.h>"
    ],
    "macosImports": [
      "<Foundation/Foundation.h>",
      "<AppKit/AppKit.h>",
      "<AgoraRtmKit/AgoraRtmKit.h>"
    ],
    "baseClass": "ViewController",
    "_ivarsComment": [
      "Declared as instance variables, not properties, because the guide pages",
      "write the bare name (`[rtm loginByToken:...]`). A @property synthesizes",
      "`_rtm`, which would not resolve `rtm`."
    ],
    "ivars": [
      { "name": "rtm", "code": "AgoraRtmClientKit *rtm;" },
      { "name": "rtmClient", "code": "AgoraRtmClientKit *rtmClient;" },
      { "name": "rtm_client", "code": "AgoraRtmClientKit *rtm_client;" }
    ],
    "properties": [
      {
        "name": "kit",
        "code": "@property (nonatomic, strong) AgoraRtmClientKit *kit;"
      },
      {
        "name": "appID",
        "code": "@property (nonatomic, strong) NSString *appID;"
      },
      {
        "name": "token",
        "code": "@property (nonatomic, strong) NSString *token;"
      },
      { "name": "uid", "code": "@property (nonatomic, strong) NSString *uid;" },
      {
        "name": "peerID",
        "code": "@property (nonatomic, strong) NSString *peerID;"
      },
      {
        "name": "channelID",
        "code": "@property (nonatomic, strong) NSString *channelID;"
      },
      {
        "name": "peerMsg",
        "code": "@property (nonatomic, strong) NSString *peerMsg;"
      },
      {
        "name": "channelMsg",
        "code": "@property (nonatomic, strong) NSString *channelMsg;"
      },
      {
        "name": "text",
        "code": "@property (nonatomic, strong) NSString *text;"
      },
      {
        "name": "textArray",
        "code": "@property (nonatomic, strong) NSMutableArray *textArray;"
      }
    ],
    "methods": [
      {
        "name": "AddMsgToRecord",
        "code": "- (void)AddMsgToRecord:(NSString *)text;"
      }
    ]
  },

  "_overridesComment": [
    "Every RTM page except the quickstart shares one running example: a client",
    "the reader already created, plus a stream channel and a listener object",
    "that sibling pages define. The guide pages and the reference pages both",
    "use it, so the shared override matches all of realtime-media/rtm/.",
    "",
    "The quickstart is the exception, because it builds its own view model and",
    "declares rtmKit as a genuine optional. Its override comes second so it",
    "wins. Overrides apply in order and the last match takes the field.",
    "",
    "The shared client is an implicitly-unwrapped optional because the docs use",
    "BOTH `rtm.getPresence()` and `rtm?.subscribe(...)`. A plain type rejects",
    "the second, an optional rejects the first, and neither page is wrong."
  ],
  "overrides": [
    {
      "match": "realtime-media/rtm/",
      "swift": {
        "fileLevel": [
          "final class RtmListener: NSObject, AgoraRtmClientDelegate {}"
        ],
        "members": [
          {
            "name": "rtmKit",
            "code": "var rtmKit: AgoraRtmClientKit! = nil"
          },
          {
            "name": "stream_channel",
            "code": "var stream_channel: AgoraRtmStreamChannel! = nil"
          },
          {
            "name": "streamChannel",
            "code": "var streamChannel: AgoraRtmStreamChannel! = nil"
          },
          { "name": "user", "code": "var user: String = \"\"" },
          { "name": "channel1", "code": "var channel1: String = \"\"" },
          { "name": "channel2", "code": "var channel2: String = \"\"" },
          {
            "name": "handler",
            "code": "var handler: RtmListener = RtmListener()"
          },
          {
            "name": "handlerEx",
            "code": "var handlerEx: RtmListener = RtmListener()"
          },
          {
            "name": "listener",
            "code": "var listener: RtmListener = RtmListener()"
          },
          {
            "name": "listenerEx",
            "code": "var listenerEx: RtmListener = RtmListener()"
          }
        ]
      },
      "objc": {
        "fileLevel": [
          {
            "name": "RtmListener",
            "code": "@interface RtmListener : NSObject <AgoraRtmClientDelegate>\n@end"
          }
        ],
        "ivars": [
          {
            "name": "stream_channel",
            "code": "AgoraRtmStreamChannel *stream_channel;"
          },
          {
            "name": "streamChannel",
            "code": "AgoraRtmStreamChannel *streamChannel;"
          },
          { "name": "handler", "code": "RtmListener *handler;" },
          { "name": "handlerEx", "code": "RtmListener *handlerEx;" },
          { "name": "listener", "code": "RtmListener *listener;" },
          { "name": "listenerEx", "code": "RtmListener *listenerEx;" }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "_comment": [
        "The quickstart is the exception: it builds its own view model, where",
        "rtmKit is a genuine optional the page declares. Applied after the",
        "shared override, so it wins."
      ],
      "match": "realtime-media/rtm/quickstart.mdx",
      "swift": {
        "members": [
          { "name": "rtmKit", "code": "var rtmKit: AgoraRtmClientKit? = nil" }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
